================================================================================
                          Improot — Authors & Contributors
================================================================================

Improot is a significant evolution of PRoot, extending it with a native
userspace virtual disk engine (libvdisk), real-time persistence, automatic
PATH discovery, and multi-format virtual drive support (QCOW2, VHD, RAW).

Improot & libvdisk — New Features, Architecture & Storage Engine:

Shubham Barman (Shado) <shubhambarman1221@gmail.com>
        Author of Improot and libvdisk. Designed and implemented the userspace
        virtual disk booting engine with support for QCOW2 v2/v3, Dynamic and
        Fixed VHD, and RAW sparse disk formats. Authored the libvdisk block,
        partition (MBR/GPT), and filesystem (ext4, FAT) driver stack. Engineered
        real-time persistence commit (--commit/--persistent), automatic binary
        directory scanner and PATH exporter (--setup-paths, -se), distro
        codename virtualization, network DNS bridging, and the structured
        Improot CLI with categorized help documentation.

================================================================================
                     PRoot & CARE — Original Authors & Credits
================================================================================

The copyright holder for PRoot and CARE is STMicroelectronics. These tools
were originally developed in the Compilation Expertise Center by:

Cédric VINCENT <cedric.vincent@st.com>
        Original author and maintainer of PRoot. Designed the core ptrace-based
        filesystem translation engine, syscall interception framework, and the
        foundational path resolution, binding, and extension systems.

Rémi DURAFFORT <remi.duraffort@st.com>
        Improved the -0 (root identity emulation) feature, conducted many
        experiments, contributed bug reports, fixes, and technical articles.

Christophe GUILLON <christophe.guillon@st.com>
        Improved CARE (Comprehensive Archiver for Reproducible Execution),
        plugin experiments, bug reports, and fixes.

Yves JANIN <yves.janin@st.com>
        Added support for the i386 architecture. Conducted many experiments
        and contributed valuable bug reports.

Antoine MOYNAULT <antoine.moynault@st.com>
        Many experiments and bug reports.

Claire ROBINE <claire.robine@st.com>
        Many bug fixes.

Clément BAZIN <clement@bazin-fr.org>
        Designed the plugins interface and dependency tracker plugin.
        Bug reports and improvements.

Christian BERTIN <christian.bertin@st.com>
        Valuable support and guidance.

